IMPORT prelude

-- Court Procedures Rules 2006 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. Periods in months and years are counted by the calendar, a day that a month lacks being the last day
-- of that month (31 August + 6 months = 28 or 29 February): fork F3 in NOTES.md. Periods in days are counted from the
-- day after the starting day (Legislation Act 2001 s 151, which the rules' Part 6.7 note names), and r 6350 (3) is
-- applied where these rules say something must or may be done within the period (fork F4): any day from 25 December to
-- 1 January is not counted. The Legislation Act s 151A (a period ending on a non-working day) is not applied: fork F5.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Court Procedures Rules 2006 (ACT)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `is on or before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
    OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same day of the month, n calendar months later; where that month is shorter, its last day (fork F3).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the clamped day` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year` MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1
        `the month length` MEANS `the days in month` `the new month` `the new year`
        `the clamped day` MEANS IF DATE_DAY `the day` GREATER THAN `the month length` THEN `the month length` ELSE DATE_DAY `the day`

-- The last day of a period of n calendar months starting on a stated day (counting that day): the day before the
-- same date n months on; where that later month lacks the date (a period starting on 29, 30 or 31 of a month), the
-- last day of that later month (fork F3). So 1 March 2027 + 12 months ends 29 February 2028, and 1 March 2027 + 6
-- months ends 31 August 2027.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `months starting on` `the start` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN DATE_DAY (`the start` `plus months` n)
    THEN `the start` `plus months` n
    ELSE (`the start` `plus months` n) `plus days` (0 MINUS 1)

-- r 6350 (3): "Any day in the period beginning on 25 December and ending on 1 January is excluded".
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Christmas-period day` `the day` IF
        (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 25)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 1)

-- The last day of a period of n days after the starting day, with the r 6350 (3) days left out of the count.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus counted days` n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `is a Christmas-period day` `the next day`
         THEN `the next day` `plus counted days` n
         ELSE `the next day` `plus counted days` (n MINUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the day` `plus days` 1
